%I A401244 #9 Oct 21 2026 20:07:38
%S A401244 77017,77041,50592937,50616073,50616121,50616143,50616359,50616617,
%T A401244 50616619,50616847,50616869,50616877,50616967,50616971,50617013,
%U A401244 50617019,50617169,50617201,50620223,50620243,50620307,50620487,50620499,50620673,50620753,50620763,50620771
%N A401244 Primes p for which pi_{24;7,17}(p) - pi_{24;1,23}(p) = -1, where pi_{m;a,b,...}(x) is the number of primes <= x which are congruent to a or b or ... (mod m).
%C A401244 Let H be a proper subgroup of (Z/NZ)* containing all the squares, and S != H be a coset of H. Assuming the generalized Riemann hypothesis (GRH) and the Grand Simplicity Hypothesis (GSH; called LI in page 29 of Greg Martin's 2010 link), then pi_{N;S}(x) > pi_{N;H}(x) occurs more often than not: the set {pi_{N;S}(x) > pi_{N;H}(x)} has logarithmic density greater than 1/2. This phenomenon is called "Chebyshev's bias".
%C A401244 Here we have N = 24, H = {1,23} and S = {7,17}. There are 11440 known terms, among which a(11427..11440) = 82458129529-82458130673 are from a single sign-changing zone. No furthur terms up to p = 1367963551751, for which pi_{24;7,17}(p) - pi_{24;1,23}(p) = 41571.
%H A401244 Jianing Song, <a href="/A401244/b401244.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..11440</a>
%H A401244 Greg Martin and Daniel Fiorilli, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Chennai-31Aug10.pdf">Prime number races: An asymptotic formula for the densities</a>, Analytic and Combinatorial Number Theory, Institute of Mathematical Sciences, Chennai, India. August 31, 2010.
%H A401244 Greg Martin, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Canberra-29Nov18.pdf">Prime number races</a>, Pure Math Seminar, UNSW Canberra. November 29, 2018.
%H A401244 Andrey S. Shchebetov, <a href="https://math101.guru/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/01-A3-Presentation-v7.3EN-no.pdf">Testing Chebyshev's bias for prime numbers up to 10^15</a>, EUCYS 2018.
%H A401244 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev%27s_bias">Chebyshev's bias</a>.
%o A401244 (PARI) my(k=0); forprime(p=2, 1e11, if(p%24==1||p%24==23, k--); if(p%24==7||p%24==17, k++); if(k==-1, print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A401244 Races between cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*:
%Y A401244 H = {1,5}: A398377 (S = {7,11}), A399143 (S = {13,17}), A399174 (S = {19,23});
%Y A401244 H = {1,13}: A297355 (S = {5,17}), A297357 (S = {7,19});
%Y A401244 H = {1,17}: A297448 (S = {5,13}), A295354 (S = {7,23});
%Y A401244 H = {1,19}: A398234 (S = {5,23}), A398235 (S = {7,13}), A398236 (S = {11,17});
%Y A401244 H = {1,23}: A401243 (S = {5,19}), this sequence (S = {7,17}), A401245 (S = {11,13}).
%K A401244 nonn,new
%O A401244 1,1
%A A401244 _Jianing Song_, Oct 18 2026
